# Second Eyes Agent Lounge — Cursor Workspace Rules

## Stack
- Cloudflare Pages + Pages Functions (NOT standalone Workers, NOT Hono)
- Functions live in `functions/` directory (plain JS, not TypeScript)
- Static assets served from `public/`
- D1 database binding is always `DB` — never `DATABASE`, never anything else
- Database name: `second-eyes-lawful-loop`

## Required reading before any edit
- `wrangler.toml` — bindings, D1 config, compatibility flags
- `public/_routes.json` — which paths hit Functions vs static
- `functions/_middleware.js` — canonical host redirect runs first

## Patterns that DO NOT apply here
- Hono router / `Hono<{ Bindings }>` generics — we don't use Hono for the lounge
- `wrangler.jsonc` — does not exist, use `wrangler.toml`
- Cloudflare AI Gateway / `cf-aig-metadata` — not in this stack
- Standalone Worker deployment — this deploys via Pages (`wrangler pages deploy`)

## Environment / secrets
- CDP keys: `CDP_API_KEY_NAME`, `CDP_API_KEY_SECRET` (Ed25519, NOT ES256)
- Payment: `X402_FACILITATOR_URL`, `X402_PAYTO`
- Auth: `ACCESS_TOKEN_SECRET`, `REVIEW_TOKEN`
- D1 accessed via `context.env.DB` in Pages Functions

## Deployment
- GitHub Actions auto-deploys on push to main
- `wrangler pages deploy public --project-name=second-eyes-ai --branch=main`
- Production SHA must match git HEAD — verify after every deploy

## Critical lessons learned
- CDP API key is Ed25519 (88-char base64) — use EdDSA/importJWK, NOT ES256/importPKCS8
- `/api/*` must bypass Cloudflare edge cache — cache rule is host-scoped to apex
- www.secondeyesai.com → 301 redirect to apex via `functions/_middleware.js`
- Discovery files cached at edge 24h, API endpoints never cached

## Product context
- Agent-only survival services lounge
- x402 USDC on Base mainnet for paid services
- Work marks sign the work, not the agent
- MCP package: `@secondeyes/mcp-unblock` in `packages/secondeye-mcp/` of this repo
